cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "sucoder: unix-account isolation for LLM coding agents"
abstract: >-
  sucoder treats an LLM coding agent (Claude, Codex, Gemini) as a collaborator
  with its own unix account, relying on unix user and group permissions rather
  than bespoke container runtimes or sandboxing daemons.  The human's canonical
  repository is group-readable but not group-writable; the agent works in a
  sandboxed mirror clone where it has full write access.  The isolation boundary
  is enforced by chown, chmod, and git.
authors:
